128	// value of each field, rejecting anything else: non-object payloads, trailing
129	// data, keys outside the allowed set, and keys that repeat after JSON
130	// unescaping. Values stay raw so each caller can decode them into pointer
131	// fields that still distinguish a missing key from an explicit null.
